EXTRA :
========================================================================================================================

.- /plots_EELS_permittivity_extra_loss_%.2f : All figures and data.
   We add an extra term for the Im(epsilon2) (which is 0.01 or 0.10)

.- plot_compare_EELS_QE_approx.py : read issue#01

.- plot_EELS_integrated_over_kx_and_1mode.py : same as before but the integral over ω is for the TM mode (highest)
         - plot EELS/L0 vs b for the highest mode: -1 is the highest (TM1), -2 is the second highest (TM2), etc..
   	[NOT USED. Fig2.]

.- /potential/old_potential: #issue03 problem with the c++ code "d.h" is solved --> old potential

.- /potential/extra: 

         - "e.h" and "e.cpp": adding a dielectric of large thickness "d". 
    	
         - plot_potential_V_V0_theta.py: find zmin(θ,V0) for fixed d (gate-waveguide distance). this executes dy.cpp
         from code c++
    	         
         - plot_potential_V_V0_d.py: find zmin(d,V0) for fixed θ_mrad
                 
         - plot_potential_num_vs_analytical.py : compare the numerical bem solution of V(z) from the c++ code
         with the analytical solution of a point charge. when d/a >> 1 (gate far from the waveguide compared to
         its size), both solutions should match. Model the potential as V(z) = V0*f(z/a)*g(d/a) with
         g(d/a) = C*log(a/2d)
                 
         - plot_analytical_correction.py : find the correction to the analytical expression that includes
         the geometry of the waveguide --> find the \Delta function, which works better for smaller height/width 
                 
         - plot_potential_with_without_substrate.py : compared the numerical with and without a substrate for
         V(z)/V0 for z>z_min = bb/2 (outside the conductor)
         
         - plot_EELS_integrated_1mode_vs_theta_parallelization.py : same as "plot_EELS_integrated_1mode_vs_theta.py" but
         finding the width for each EELS and parallelizing (works in Windows: for the Rocket). not need at the end because
         in windows the parallelization is really slow. 

         - plot_EELS_integrated_over_z_vs_omega.py : use the bem2d files for EELS per unit length per unit eV to integrated
         the trajectory of the electron (from zmin(θ,V0) to infty) in combination with dz/V(z)... from c++ code (see
         definition written in "Eq_P_integral_over_z.png"). [NOT USED]
         
